This is the actual proof of the work: not “a file exists,” but every single keystroke and mouse movement that produced it, timestamped to the millisecond and hash-chained. You can’t fake the process the way you can fake the product — and a back-dated file would leave no trail of how it was typed.

Every entry is append-only & hash-chained — work, milestones, and spend in one signed record. Nothing can be edited, deleted, or back-dated. It’s your research timeline and your grant ledger — no separate accounting software.

Built for the researcher — and the institution behind them
The researcher owns their credit and priority; the institution owns its integrity and reputation. A leak or a disputed claim hurts both. WorkSigned protects both, as equals.

Protect the intellectual property
Whatever the ownership split, the work needs a tamper-evident chain of custody — provable provenance for the researcher’s contribution, a defensible asset for the institution.

Defend attribution & priority
The record shows who did what and when, down to the individual — provable authorship for the researcher, fewer conflicts for the institution.

Guard reputation
Stealth research and exfiltration countermeasures keep sensitive work confidential — no leak before you choose to announce it.

Answer to grants & audits
Every deliverable — and every dollar — on the same signed timeline: what was done, by whom, and at what cost, tied to the grants that funded it. Funders and auditors pull one tamper-evident trail — and you stop paying for a separate grant-accounting tool to do it.

One platform. Every tool you work in.
Code, email, documents, spreadsheets, presentations, LaTeX, AI chat, many more scientific applications — not bolted-on plugins, but native tools that all write to the same signed record. And code you write in the editor runs right in the platform.

